# Root .dockerignore — build context for the API image (context = repo root,
# needed so pnpm workspace deps in packages/core resolve). Keeps the context
# small and avoids leaking secrets/editor state into the build.

# VCS / editor / agent state
**/.git
**/.gitignore
.github
.claude
.vscode
.idea
**/.DS_Store

# Node / pnpm build artifacts (rebuilt inside the image)
**/node_modules
**/.pnpm-store
**/dist
**/.next
**/out
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# ADR-0014: moon's cache is machine-local and not portable across
# environments (see moonrepo.dev/docs/guides/docker) -- must never be
# COPY'd into a build context.
.moon/cache

# Python artifacts — irrelevant to the API image, excluded for size
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache

# Secrets — never send into a build context
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Logs
**/*.log

# ADR-0014 (2026-10-03): the old hand-maintained exclusion list for
# "workspace members not needed to build @fact-checker-ke/api" (apps,
# services/pipeline, docs, db) was removed here. That list is exactly the
# hard-coded dependency graph ADR-0014 exists to eliminate -- it broke once
# already when packages/db landed and services/api started depending on it.
# services/api/Dockerfile's "skeleton" stage now needs the full workspace
# in its build context so `moon docker scaffold api` can derive the real
# dependency graph; `pnpm deploy --prod` (also in that Dockerfile -- see
# its DEVIATION 3 comment) is what keeps the final runtime image small,
# not this file.
